  "design_conclusion": {
    "supported": "A SYN-only, interface-bound inbound state created before connection birth preserves that connection across a later outgoing deny. The chosen old-outbound reply does not acquire reverse permission; loopback no-state override permits listener closure.",
    "limitation": "Adding tracking after connection birth does not preserve the existing untracked session. This partial solution does not by itself meet a guarantee for startup, Stop/reactivation or lost PF state.",
    "recommended_next_step": "Design explicit ordinary-Direct tracking versus fully released Stop/uninstall, current-policy health/readback, owned-state cleanup and startup limits before implementing an application change."
  },
